## Comprehensive `meshDict` example

The following example collects the major cfMesh and CFMitch controls used during development of this OpenFOAM Foundation 13 fork.

It is intended as a **reference configuration**, not as a recommended configuration for every geometry. Many of the controls are experimental, geometry-specific, legacy, diagnostic, or mutually exclusive.

For new difficult boundary-layer cases, the recommended starting point is generally:

```text
boundaryLayerArchitecture constraintPlanner;
autoDetectBoundaryJunctions true;
cfmitchV10KCrossPatchLayerSync true;
cfmitchV9MergePeriodicFaceFans true;
```

with other repair or diagnostic mechanisms enabled only when required.

```cpp
FoamFile
{
    version   2.0;
    format    ascii;
    class     dictionary;
    location  "system";
    object    meshDict;
}


// ============================================================================
// GENERAL DIAGNOSTICS
// ============================================================================

// Optional lineage diagnostics.
writeLineageDiagnostics false;

writeLineageStages
(
    postBLCreate
    postOptimize
    postRefBL
    final
);


// ============================================================================
// INPUT GEOMETRY
// ============================================================================

surfaceFile "constant/triSurface/Rotor37_cfmesh.stl";


// ============================================================================
// BASE CARTESIAN MESH
// ============================================================================

maxCellSize       0.003;
boundaryCellSize  0.001;
minCellSize       0.0005;

// Point known to lie inside the fluid domain.
insideMesh (0.214 0.000 0.025);


// ============================================================================
// SURFACE REFINEMENT
// ============================================================================

localRefinement
{
    blade_1
    {
        cellSize 0.0005;
    }

    blade_2
    {
        cellSize 0.0005;
    }

    blade_3
    {
        cellSize 0.0005;
    }

    blade_4
    {
        cellSize 0.0005;
    }

    hub
    {
        cellSize 0.001;
    }

    shroud
    {
        cellSize 0.001;
    }

    periodic_1
    {
        cellSize 0.0005;
    }

    periodic_2
    {
        cellSize 0.0005;
    }
}


// ============================================================================
// OPTIONAL VOLUMETRIC / OBJECT REFINEMENT
// ============================================================================

objectRefinements
{
    fineBox
    {
        type      box;
        centre    (0.214 0.0 0.025);

        lengthX   0.20;
        lengthY   0.10;
        lengthZ   0.10;

        cellSize  0.0005;
    }

    transitionBox
    {
        type      box;
        centre    (0.214 0.0 0.025);

        lengthX   0.30;
        lengthY   0.15;
        lengthZ   0.15;

        cellSize  0.001;
    }
}


// ============================================================================
// OPTIONAL GEOMETRY PREPROCESSING
// ============================================================================

geometryPreprocessing
{
    active                true;
    reportOnly            false;

    weldNearPoints        false;
    selectiveWeld         false;

    weldTolerance         1e-4;

    autoScaleWithCellSize false;
    minFeatureToCellRatio 0.20;

    writeDiagnostics      false;
}


// ============================================================================
// GLOBAL RECOVERY / EXPERIMENTAL CONTROLS
// ============================================================================

// Number of negative-volume cells which may be considered recoverable by
// selected repair stages.
dirtyRecoverableMaxNegVol 10;

// Experimental triple-junction smoother.
enableRung2TJSmoother true;

// Experimental post-BL rescue path.
enablePostBLRescue true;

// Number of rings available to the rung-2 repair mechanism.
rung2MaxRings 4;


// ============================================================================
// BOUNDARY LAYERS
// ============================================================================

boundaryLayers
{
    // ========================================================================
    // BL ARCHITECTURE
    // ========================================================================

    // Available development architectures:
    //
    // classicCfMesh
    // legacyEnhanced
    // constraintPlanner
    //
    // constraintPlanner is the current primary development architecture.

    boundaryLayerArchitecture constraintPlanner;


    // ========================================================================
    // CONSTRAINT PLANNER
    // ========================================================================

    constraintPlanner
    {
        // Maximum permitted neighboring layer-count difference.
        maxLayerStep 2;

        // Minimum neutral-boundary projection scaling.
        neutralProjectionFloor 0.0;

        heightPlanner
        {
            enabled          false;

            maxEdgeRatio     1.50;
            maxMoveFraction  0.05;
            iterations       1;
        }
    }


    // ========================================================================
    // PRE-REFINEMENT COUPLED BL OPTIMISATION
    // ========================================================================

    // Experimental coupled one-layer optimiser.
    cfmitchPreRefBLCoupledOptimisation false;

    // Actually commit the coupled optimiser result.
    cfmitchPreRefBLCoupledCommit false;

    cfmitchPreRefBLMinHairRatio 0.50;

    cfmitchPreRefBLNormalSmoothingIterations 2;


    // ========================================================================
    // AUTOMATIC BOUNDARY-JUNCTION DISCOVERY
    // ========================================================================

    // Automatically classify multi-patch boundary junctions from actual
    // topology and resolved BL intent.
    //
    // This replaces the need for some geometry-specific hard-coded
    // triple-junction definitions.
    autoDetectBoundaryJunctions true;


    // ========================================================================
    // SHARP-EDGE / FEATURE CONTROLS
    // ========================================================================

    blSharpEdgeAngleDeg 85;

    blblFeatureAngleDeg      35.0;
    blblCornerAcuteThreshold 0.5;

    lockAcuteCornerPoints true;


    // ========================================================================
    // ACUTE-CORNER LOCAL TAPER
    // ========================================================================

    acuteCornerRing0 0.00;
    acuteCornerRing1 0.02;
    acuteCornerRing2 0.05;
    acuteCornerRing3 0.15;
    acuteCornerRing4 0.35;
    acuteCornerRing5 0.60;
    acuteCornerRing6 1.00;

    acuteCornerCapLayers false;


    // ========================================================================
    // PATCH ROLES
    // ========================================================================

    patchRoles
    {
        wall
        (
            blade_1
            blade_2
            blade_3
            blade_4
            hub
            shroud
        );

        blade
        (
            blade_1
            blade_2
            blade_3
            blade_4
        );

        hub
        (
            hub
        );

        shroud
        (
            shroud
        );

        periodic
        (
            periodic_1
            periodic_2
        );

        inletOutlet
        (
            inlet
            outlet
        );
    }


    // ========================================================================
    // BL TERMINATION PATCHES
    // ========================================================================

    terminationPatches
    (
        inlet
        outlet
    );


    // ========================================================================
    // CONTACT-LINE POLICY
    // ========================================================================

    useContactLinePolicy true;

    useContactLineHeightSmoother true;

    writeContactLineHeightSmootherAtlas true;

    contactLineSmootherMaxGrowth       1.5;
    contactLineSmootherMinCollapse     0.05;
    contactLineSmootherMaxMoveFraction 0.25;
    contactLineSmootherIterations      1;
    contactLineSmootherMinHeight       1e-8;


    // ========================================================================
    // HARD BL/BL JUNCTION HANDLING
    // ========================================================================

    useHardBLBLCapCells             true;
    useHardBLBLCapVertexInsertion   true;
    useHardBLBLReducedCells         true;
    useHardBLBLAsymmetricCapFaces   false;

    hardBLBLCapScale 0.10;


    // ========================================================================
    // LEGACY / EXPLICIT TRIPLE-JUNCTION CONTROLS
    // ========================================================================

    // These remain useful for explicit geometry-specific control, although
    // autoDetectBoundaryJunctions is preferred where topology can determine
    // the relationship automatically.

    tripleJunctionSuppressPatches
    (
        hub
        shroud
    );

    tripleJunctionFaceRingExclusion true;

    tripleJunctionProtectedRing0Scale 0.5;

    tripleJunctionWallPatches
    (
        blade_1
        blade_2
        blade_3
        blade_4
    );

    tripleJunctionNeutralPatches
    (
        periodic_1
        periodic_2
    );


    // ========================================================================
    // VIRTUAL-TOPOLOGY EXCLUSION
    // ========================================================================

    virtualTopologyExclusion true;

    virtualTopoRing0 0.05;
    virtualTopoRing1 0.15;
    virtualTopoRing2 0.40;


    // ========================================================================
    // PERIODIC TRANSITION PROTECTION
    // ========================================================================

    periodicTransitionProtection true;

    periodicTransitionSkipFlip true;

    periodicTransitionPatches
    (
        periodic_1
        periodic_2
    );


    // ========================================================================
    // CFMITCH PERIODIC FACE-FAN REPAIR
    // ========================================================================

    // Proven periodic face-fan reconstruction used in the Rotor37 v1.0.0
    // regression.
    cfmitchV9MergePeriodicFaceFans true;


    // ========================================================================
    // CROSS-PATCH BL LAYER SYNCHRONISATION
    // ========================================================================

    // Older skew-driven experimental retreat path.
    cfmitchV10GCrossPatchSkewRetreat false;

    // Current final-layer-count reconciliation across real BL/BL patch seams.
    // This was required to eliminate the remaining internal Rotor37
    // cross-patch skew failures.
    cfmitchV10KCrossPatchLayerSync true;


    // ========================================================================
    // PERIODIC NORMAL-REJECTION PROOF / COMMIT
    // ========================================================================

    // Diagnostic proof stage.
    cfmitchV11BProbeNormalRejected true;

    // Commit only normal-rejected periodic repairs which pass the proof.
    cfmitchV11CCommitProvenNormalRejected true;


    // ========================================================================
    // GAP / CLEARANCE DETECTION
    // ========================================================================

    // Current gap handling uses explicit patch pairs.
    //
    // This is NOT yet a complete automatic turbomachinery tip-clearance
    // planner.

    detectGaps true;

    gapThreshold 1e-5;

    gapPatchPairs
    (
        (blade_1 shroud)
        (blade_2 shroud)
        (blade_3 shroud)
        (blade_4 shroud)
    );

    gapSuppressPatches
    (
        shroud
        hub
    );


    // ========================================================================
    // GAP CONFLICT ARBITRATION
    // ========================================================================

    gapConflictMode autoThickness;

    gapLoserRing1Suppress false;

    gapLoserRing1MaxLayers 3;
    gapLoserRing2MaxLayers 3;

    blTerminationRing1MaxLayers 3;
    blTerminationRing2MaxLayers 3;


    // ========================================================================
    // GAP FACE-RING EXCLUSION / TAPER
    // ========================================================================

    gapFaceRingExclusion true;

    gapFaceRing0Scale 0.02;
    gapFaceRing1Scale 0.05;
    gapFaceRing2Scale 0.20;
    gapFaceRing3Scale 0.50;


    // ========================================================================
    // POST-OPTIMIZER BL RETRACTION
    // ========================================================================

    postOptBLRetraction false;

    postOptBLRetractionRings 1;


    // ========================================================================
    // PRE-refBL SNAPSHOT
    // ========================================================================

    // Save the valid mesh state before refineLayers().
    //
    // Required for the current transactional two-pass repair mechanism.

    preRefBLSnapshot true;


    // ========================================================================
    // TRANSACTIONAL POST-refBL REPAIR
    // ========================================================================

    // Preferred mechanism:
    //
    // Pass 1:
    //   refine BL
    //   detect hard failures
    //   trace failure provenance
    //
    // Pass 2:
    //   restore snapshot
    //   apply locally modified BL constraints
    //   regenerate BL
    //
    // Commit only if the candidate is safer.

    preRefBLAutoRepair true;


    // ========================================================================
    // LEGACY FILE-BASED PROVENANCE REPLAY
    // ========================================================================

    // Debug/replay mechanism only.
    //
    // Do not normally combine this with preRefBLAutoRepair.

    postRefBLProvenanceRetraction false;

    postRefBLProvenanceSeedFile
        postRefBL_provenanceSeedBfI.labels;


    // ========================================================================
    // PROVENANCE REPAIR RINGS
    // ========================================================================

    postRefBLRing0MaxLayers 3;
    postRefBLRing1MaxLayers 4;
    postRefBLRing2MaxLayers 0;

    postRefBLRing0ThicknessScale 0.60;
    postRefBLRing1ThicknessScale 0.80;
    postRefBLRing2ThicknessScale 1.00;


    // ========================================================================
    // PROSPECTIVE FRONT CAPS
    // ========================================================================

    // Current prospective safe-depth reconstruction / cap mechanism.
    cfmitchV52bApplyFrontCaps true;


    // ========================================================================
    // QUAD-FAN ESCAPE
    // ========================================================================

    // Converts selected problematic internal quads into a face-centre fan.
    //
    // Development implementation is intended for deterministic serial/OMP1
    // operation.
    cfmitchV57QuadFanEscape true;


    // ========================================================================
    // LAYER OPTIMISATION
    // ========================================================================

    optimiseLayer       false;
    optimiseLayerBuffer false;

    postRefineBLOptimisation true;


    // ========================================================================
    // SURFACE-CONSTRAINED OPTIMIZER
    // ========================================================================

    constrainOptimizerBoundaryMotion true;


    // ========================================================================
    // LIMITED POST-OPTIMIZER REPROJECTION
    // ========================================================================

    postOptimizerReprojStepFraction 0.005;

    postOptimizerReprojPasses 10;


    // ========================================================================
    // POST-BL SNAP
    // ========================================================================

    postBLSnap true;

    postBLSnapTolerance 1e-4;

    postBLSnapAllowedPyramidIncrease 25;

    postBLSnapAllowedPyramidIncreaseFraction 0.001;


    // ========================================================================
    // SNAP CONTROLS
    // ========================================================================

    cornerSnapRelaxation 0.25;
    cornerSnapIterations 1;

    edgeSnapRelaxation   1.0;
    edgeSnapIterations   1;

    snapMinPyramidHeight 1e-10;


    // ========================================================================
    // BL TRANSITION TAPER
    // ========================================================================

    layerScaleRing1 0.25;
    layerScaleRing2 0.50;
    layerScaleRing3 0.45;
    layerScaleRing4 0.65;
    layerScaleRing5 0.80;
    layerScaleRing6 1.00;

    flowTerminationTaperFloor   0.25;
    periodicNeutralTaperFloor   0.20;


    // ========================================================================
    // OPTIONAL BL/BL JUNCTION LAYER-COUNT RAMP
    // ========================================================================

    enableBlblJunctionLayerCountRamp false;


    // ========================================================================
    // GLOBAL DEFAULT BL PARAMETERS
    // ========================================================================

    // Global default. Setting nLayers=0 allows patchBoundaryLayers to define
    // the active BL surfaces individually.

    nLayers 0;

    thicknessRatio 1.30;

    maxFirstLayerThickness 1e-4;


    // ========================================================================
    // PATCH-SPECIFIC BL PARAMETERS
    // ========================================================================

    patchBoundaryLayers
    {
        blade_1
        {
            nLayers                15;
            thicknessRatio         1.30;
            maxFirstLayerThickness 5e-5;
        }

        blade_2
        {
            nLayers                15;
            thicknessRatio         1.30;
            maxFirstLayerThickness 5e-5;
        }

        blade_3
        {
            nLayers                15;
            thicknessRatio         1.30;
            maxFirstLayerThickness 5e-5;
        }

        blade_4
        {
            nLayers                15;
            thicknessRatio         1.30;
            maxFirstLayerThickness 5e-5;
        }

        hub
        {
            nLayers                15;
            thicknessRatio         1.30;
            maxFirstLayerThickness 1e-4;
        }

        shroud
        {
            nLayers                15;
            thicknessRatio         1.30;
            maxFirstLayerThickness 1e-4;
        }

        inlet
        {
            nLayers 0;
        }

        outlet
        {
            nLayers 0;
        }

        periodic_1
        {
            nLayers 0;
        }

        periodic_2
        {
            nLayers 0;
        }
    }
}


// ============================================================================
// BOUNDARY RENAMING
// ============================================================================

renameBoundary
{
    defaultName walls;
    defaultType wall;

    newPatchNames
    {
        inlet
        {
            newName inlet;
            type    patch;
        }

        outlet
        {
            newName outlet;
            type    patch;
        }

        hub
        {
            newName hub;
            type    wall;
        }

        shroud
        {
            newName shroud;
            type    wall;
        }

        periodic_1
        {
            newName periodic_1;
            type    patch;
        }

        periodic_2
        {
            newName periodic_2;
            type    patch;
        }

        blade_1
        {
            newName blade_1;
            type    wall;
        }

        blade_2
        {
            newName blade_2;
            type    wall;
        }

        blade_3
        {
            newName blade_3;
            type    wall;
        }

        blade_4
        {
            newName blade_4;
            type    wall;
        }
    }
}
```

### Important notes

Several controls above should **not simply be enabled together because they exist**.

In particular:

- `preRefBLAutoRepair` is the preferred transactional repair mechanism.
- `postRefBLProvenanceRetraction` is an older manual/replay mechanism and should normally remain disabled.
- `cfmitchV10GCrossPatchSkewRetreat` is an older experimental approach; `cfmitchV10KCrossPatchLayerSync` is the preferred seam-layer reconciliation mechanism.
- `cfmitchV11BProbeNormalRejected` is diagnostic/proof infrastructure; `cfmitchV11CCommitProvenNormalRejected` performs the corresponding proof-gated commit.
- `gapPatchPairs` are still manually specified. Automatic topological junction discovery does not yet automatically solve non-touching blade-tip/shroud clearances.
- `cfmitchV57QuadFanEscape` is a specialized repair mechanism and should not be treated as a universally required option.
- `OMP_NUM_THREADS=1` remains the recommended deterministic development/regression mode.

This sample should therefore be treated as a **control reference**, not a recommendation to turn every switch on.
